    {
      "id": 130357,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-03T18:52:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Two cards from the same deck aren't nemeses either, right? &nbsp;For things like the Ennead, the Chairman/Operative, and the Sentinels.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes they can be. If Operative dealt the Chairman damage, it would be increased due to the nemesis bonus. Ennead members are the same way.</p>\n<p><em>Any</em> <em>different card</em> that shares a nemesis symbol would get the bonus damage applied to them, even if they come from the same deck.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:05:28.148Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
